<%# locals: (task:, agents:, variant: :stack, events: nil, mascot: nil, board: :deploy) %>
<%#
  The line above is a Rails strict-locals signature, so Rails itself supplies every
  default — `variant` is :stack, `events`/`mascot` are nil, and `board` is :deploy —
  without any local_assigns.fetch. `mascot` is the one exception that still reads
  through local_assigns below (line 27): its default must differ per caller — the
  board passes a preloaded mascot (which may be nil), while the detail page omits it
  and falls back to a DB lookup. (Strict-locals defaults are NOT keys in
  local_assigns, so that fetch block genuinely runs when mascot is omitted.)

  Per-stage agent attribution across a task's WHOLE journey — who designed, built,
  submitted, reviewed, assembled, and shipped it, with the time each stage took.

  Source: stage_agent_groups(task, agents) reads the task's TaskEvents +
  (review only) reviewers metadata (see StageAgentsHelper). Build-lane stages show
  the event's actor (the feature agent); reviewed shows the 2 senior reviewers;
  assembled shows Steffon; shipped shows Avi. A task renders nothing only when it
  has no stage events with a crew to attribute — the partial then renders nothing
  at all (no empty container).

  variant:
    :stack    (default) one near-fully stacked circle per lane (Build · Review ·
              Deploy) carrying that lane's duration or a live build counter — the
              board card glance; the lane row flex-wraps so a full crew never
              spills a narrow column.
    :detailed grouped per stage with a studio-engine badge, names, weights, and
              the full humanized duration — the task detail.

  Avatars are theme-token only (ring-surface separators, surface-alt pills) so
  dark/light parity holds; faces reuse the components/agent_avatar primitive
  (image with a deterministic initials fallback).
%>
<%# Build-lane crew wears the task's mascot. Callers (the board) pass it from a
    preloaded map to avoid an N+1; the detail page resolves it here. %>
<% mascot = local_assigns.fetch(:mascot) { Pokemon.find_by(slug: task.devops["mascot"].to_s.presence) } %>
<% entries = stage_agent_groups(task, agents, events: events, mascot: mascot) %>
<% if stage_crew_renderable?(task, entries, mascot: mascot, variant: variant, board: board) %>
  <% if variant.to_sym == :detailed %>
    <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-lg p-3" data-test="stage-agent-avatars">
      <p class="label-upper mb-3">Stage crew</p>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <% entries.group_by(&:stage).each do |stage, stage_entries| %>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
            <%= render "components/badge", text: Task::STAGE_LABELS.fetch(stage, stage.humanize), scheme: stage_scheme(stage) %>
            <% stage_entries.each do |entry| %>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                <div class="relative rounded-full ring-2 ring-surface">
                  <%= render "components/agent_avatar", agent: entry, size: "xs" %>
                </div>
                <div class="leading-tight">
                  <p class="text-sm text-heading flex items-center gap-1.5">
                    <%= entry.name %>
                    <% if entry.weight.present? %>
                      <span class="px-1 py-px rounded text-[9px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide
                                   <%= entry.primary? ? 'bg-primary/15 text-primary border border-primary/30' : 'bg-surface text-muted border border-subtle' %>"
                            title="<%= entry.primary? ? 'Primary (deep) review' : 'Light review' %>">
                        <%= entry.role_label %>
                      </span>
                    <% end %>
                  </p>
                  <% if (spent = humanize_stage_duration(entry.seconds)) %>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted"><%= spent %> in <%= entry.from_label %></p>
                  <% end %>
                </div>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <%#
      Board-card glance (a dashboard, not the read view): collapse each lane to ONE
      stacked circle — Build · Review · Deploy — so a full crew fits a small card;
      the row also flex-wraps as a final guard against spilling a narrow column.
      Each cluster stacks its faces (priority on top) and shows the one duration that
      matters for the lane (build total / longer review / QA→prod). The build lane
      ticks a LIVE counter only while the task is actively `building` (a real claim) —
      a `designed`/unclaimed card shows its mascot with no ticker. The detail page
      (:detailed) still shows every stage per-usual.
    %>
    <% columns = crew_columns(task, entries, board: board, mascot: mascot, agents: agents, events: events) %>
    <%# Crew avatars are one large size on both boards (md = w-14 face, -space-x-10 =
        40px overlap → 16px peek) so they fill the 3-slot grid instead of floating in
        empty space. Uniform size means a 3-slot and a 4-slot card keep the same avatar
        height and their rows line up across lanes. Hover/focus keeps the under-stack
        fixed, scales only the lead face, and nudges the first/last filled lead faces
        outward so the motion is intentional. %>
    <%# 4-slot cards (assembled/shipped) pack more faces, so they run a size smaller
        than the roomier 3-slot cards. The crew band below is a fixed h-14 with the
        stacks vertically centered, so shrinking the 4-slot faces never breaks the row
        alignment across lanes — the smaller faces just center in the same band. %>
    <% four_slot = columns.size == 4 %>
    <% crew_size = four_slot ? "sm" : "md" %>
    <%# Under-stack faces drop one more size and the overlap tightens to match — a
        smaller face under a wide overlap would vanish behind the lead — leaving each a
        small ~8px peek so the back stack tucks tightly to the left. %>
    <% crew_under_size = four_slot ? "xs" : "sm" %>
    <% crew_overlap = four_slot ? "-space-x-6" : "-space-x-8" %>
    <% crew_empty_dims = four_slot ? "w-10 h-10" : "w-14 h-14" %>
    <% crew_top_reveal = "transition-transform duration-200 ease-out group-hover:scale-150 group-focus-within:scale-150 hover:scale-150 motion-reduce:transition-none motion-reduce:transform-none" %>
    <%# A blocked card reads design · building · blocker; the blocker is the LAST
        filled compartment (slot 3), and its timer turns into a red ✕. %>
    <% blocked = task.blocked? %>
    <% block_idx = (columns.rindex { |c| c.stacked.any? } if blocked) %>
    <% last_filled_idx = columns.rindex { |c| c.stacked.any? } %>
    <%# EXPERIMENTAL hover reveal (see the promote render in the empty-slot branch):
        active ONLY for the exact shape — 3 slots, an empty 3rd slot, and a 2nd slot
        holding a pair. On card hover, slot 2's under-face ("2.2") jumps into the empty
        slot 3. promote_entry is that under-face (stacked.first, since the lead renders
        last); nil disables the whole feature for every other layout. %>
    <% promote_entry = (columns.size == 3 && columns[2] && !columns[2].stacked.any? &&
                        columns[1] && columns[1].stacked.size == 2) ? columns[1].stacked.first : nil %>
    <%# Fixed grid (3 columns, or 4 on the assembled + shipped columns) so the crew is
        one solid row; each compartment centered in its column, an unreached stage left
        blank. On an assembled card the fourth slot is reserved (empty placeholder, or
        Avi's live deploy intent) so the card never reflows when it ships. The Build
        board (/tasks) splits the build steps; Deploy collapses them — except a blocked
        card, which splits back to design · building · blocker on both boards. %>
    <div class="grid grid-rows-1 items-center h-14 <%= columns.size == 4 ? 'grid-cols-4' : 'grid-cols-3' %> gap-1 mt-3 mb-1"
         data-test="stage-agent-avatars" title="Stage crew">
      <% columns.each_with_index do |cluster, ci| %>
        <%# Filled compartments hug the left (the real crew); an empty slot centers in
            its column so the dashed placeholders read as a tidy centered row. %>
        <div class="flex <%= cluster.stacked.any? ? "justify-start" : "justify-center" %>">
          <% if cluster.stacked.any? %>
            <div class="relative" data-test="crew-cluster" data-lane="<%= cluster.lane %>">
              <%# Stack runs lead-FIRST (highest on the LEFT): the lead is leftmost and lifted
                  (z-30) so its glow sits on top; the next gets a subtler ring; deeper avatars
                  blend and peek out to the right. The stack spacing stays fixed on
                  hover/focus; the lead face is the only avatar that scales, with the
                  row edges nudged outward by 12px. %>
              <%# Alignment map: 3 slots = left / center / right; 4 slots = left /
                  center / center / right. These are transform origins; filled clusters
                  still start from the left edge of their grid cell. %>
              <% crew_pos = if ci.zero?
                              "origin-left"
                            elsif ci == columns.size - 1
                              "origin-right"
                            else
                              "origin-center"
                            end %>
              <%# Bottom-align the stack so the smaller under-faces sit LOW (their base
                  on the lead's base) and peek from the bottom-right, not floating at
                  the lead's vertical center. %>
              <div class="flex items-end <%= crew_overlap %> <%= crew_pos %>"
                   data-test="crew-stack">
                <% cluster.stacked.reverse.each_with_index do |entry, i| %>
                  <% stack_position = i.zero? ? "top" : "under" %>
                  <% edge_reveal = if ci.zero?
                                     "origin-left group-hover:-translate-x-3 group-focus-within:-translate-x-3 hover:-translate-x-3"
                                   elsif ci == last_filled_idx
                                     "origin-right group-hover:translate-x-3 group-focus-within:translate-x-3 hover:translate-x-3"
                                   else
                                     "origin-center"
                                   end %>
                  <%# When this cluster is the promote source (slot 2's pair), its under-face
                      slides right and fades out on hover — it "leaves" for slot 3. %>
                  <% promote_out = (promote_entry && ci == 1 && i == 1) ? " transition-all duration-200 group-hover:opacity-0 group-hover:translate-x-4" : "" %>
                  <div class="rounded-full relative ring-2 <%= i == 0 ? "z-30 ring-primary/70 #{crew_top_reveal} #{edge_reveal}" : (i == 1 ? "z-20 ring-primary/50" : "z-10 ring-surface") %><%= promote_out %>"
                       title="<%= [entry.name, (entry.role_label.presence && "(#{entry.role_label})")].compact.join(' ') %>"
                       data-test="crew-stack-avatar"
                       data-stack-position="<%= stack_position %>">
                    <%= render "components/agent_avatar", agent: entry,
                          size: (i.zero? ? crew_size : crew_under_size),
                          shiny: (false unless i.zero?) %>
                  </div>
                <% end %>
              </div>
              <% if blocked && ci == block_idx %>
                <%# Blocked here — the latest agent's timer becomes a red ✕. %>
                <span class="absolute -bottom-1 -left-1 z-40 px-1 py-px rounded-full text-[10px] font-bold leading-none
                             bg-red-500/30 text-red-200 border border-red-400/70 ring-1 ring-surface"
                      data-test="crew-blocked" title="Blocked at this stage">✕</span>
              <% elsif cluster.live_since %>
                <%# Live elapsed counter (s → m → h → d → w), ticking each second. %>
                <span class="absolute -bottom-1 -left-1 z-40 px-1 py-px rounded-full text-[9px] font-semibold leading-none
                             bg-green-500/30 text-green-100 border border-green-400/60 ring-1 ring-surface tabular-nums animate-pulse"
                      data-test="crew-live"
                      x-data="{ start: <%= cluster.live_since.to_i %>, now: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) }"
                      x-init="setInterval(() => now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000), 1000)"
                      x-text="window.elapsedLabel(now - start)">…</span>
              <% elsif cluster.seconds.to_i.positive? %>
                <span class="absolute -bottom-1 -left-1 z-40 px-1 py-px rounded-full text-[9px] font-semibold leading-none
                             bg-surface-alt text-secondary border border-subtle ring-1 ring-surface tabular-nums"
                      data-test="crew-duration"><%= compact_stage_duration(cluster.seconds) %></span>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          <% elsif promote_entry && ci == 2 %>
            <%# Promote target: the empty 3rd slot. The dashed placeholder fades out and
                the promoted "2.2" face slides in from slot 2's side and fades in — so on
                hover the pair in slot 2 splits into three across the row. %>
            <div class="relative <%= crew_empty_dims %>" data-test="crew-promote-slot">
              <div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-full border-2 border-dashed border-white/15 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-0"
                   data-test="crew-empty" data-lane="<%= cluster.lane %>"></div>
              <div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center origin-right opacity-0 -translate-x-3 scale-75 transition-all duration-200 ease-out group-hover:opacity-100 group-hover:translate-x-0 group-hover:scale-150"
                   data-test="crew-promoted" aria-hidden="true">
                <%# Rendered at the LEAD size (md) and scaled up from ~the under-size it
                    left as, all the way to the lead's 150% hover reveal, so it grows into
                    a full third crew member that matches the enlarged leads on hover.
                    origin-right keeps the grow on-card at the right edge. %>
                <div class="rounded-full ring-2 ring-primary/70">
                  <%= render "components/agent_avatar", agent: promote_entry, size: crew_size %>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          <% else %>
            <%# Unreached pipeline stage — a dashed placeholder circle marks the slot. %>
            <div class="rounded-full border-2 border-dashed border-white/15 <%= crew_empty_dims %>"
                 data-test="crew-empty" data-lane="<%= cluster.lane %>"></div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
